   "gap": "Three source variants are narrowed. Durrett (pp. 16-17) defines almost sure convergence without a prescribed limit (X_n converges a.s. when P(Omega_o) = 1 for Omega_o the event that lim X_n exists; almost everywhere convergence in measure theory) and takes X_infinity = limsup X_n, possibly infinite, as the limit; the entry defines a.s. convergence only toward a specified real random variable. Durrett's extended-valued random variables may have any domain D in F; the entry requires domain Omega. Durrett equips [-infinity, infinity] with the Borel sets of its usual topology (generated by [-infinity, a), (a, b), (b, infinity]); the entry uses the sigma-algebra generated by [-infinity, a] without showing that the two coincide.",
